==Battleground==
*2 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**5 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**4 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Lord Gravey as a boss in a limited cash stage is brutal, as is the choice of main supporting peon in Jackrabbits to slip in after Gravey attacks and snipe your attackers. As if keeping enough DPS alive wasn't hard enough, a Bore spawns partway into the boss wave to try and kill your stack. Oh, and the stage starts with a Jackrabbit and Zang Roo right away in case you thought you could stall for cooldowns.

[[Fried Chicken Cat]] not only has respectable DPS, but also inflicts Curse so Shigong can deal damage on Gravey. [[Manic Island Cat|Manic Island]] is also [[Strong Against]] Red, who works well with [[Courier Cat]] against Jackrabbit and Bore, as Manic Island can keep the enemies outside of Courier's blindspot for Courier to nuke them. [[Talent|Talented]] [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used to deal with the Bore quicker.

If Lord Gravey wasn't [[Zombie Killer|Z-killed]], reset your run, as by that point you should have been broke with no cash left to deal with it.

